{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "\n",
        "book:\n",
        "  title: \"Hands-On Programming with R\"\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "```{css}\n",
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "/* In a .css file or in a code cell */\n",
        ".rendered .cell-output-display,\n",
        ".graphviz {\n",
        "  page-break-inside: avoid !important;\n",
        "  break-inside: avoid-page !important;\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "/* Or target the container more specifically */\n",
        "div.cell-output-display {\n",
        "  page-break-before: avoid;\n",
        "  page-break-after: avoid;\n",
        "  page-break-inside: avoid;\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1\n",
        "## a\n",
        "### Entity Sets\n",
        "\n",
        "- Account\n",
        "- Branch\n",
        "- Customer\n",
        "- Loan\n",
        "\n",
        "### Relations\n",
        "\n",
        "- Account branch\n",
        "\n",
        ">> Many Accounts to One Branch with all Accounts needing to have a branch\n",
        "\n",
        "- Loan branch\n",
        "\n",
        ">> Many Loans to One Branch with all Loans needing to have a branch\n",
        "\n",
        "- Depositor\n",
        "\n",
        ">> Accounts to Customer\n",
        "\n",
        "- Borrower\n",
        "\n",
        ">> Customer to Loan\n",
        "\n",
        "## b\n",
        "### Entities\n",
        "Account(<u>Account_No</u>, Balance, B_name)\n",
        "\n",
        "Branch(<u>B_name</u>, B_city, Assets)\n",
        "\n",
        "Customer(<u>C_name</u>, C_city, C_street)\n",
        "\n",
        "Loan(<u>Loan_No</u>, Amount, B_name)\n",
        "\n",
        "### Relations\n",
        "Depositor(<u>Account_No,C_name</u>)\n",
        "\n",
        "Borrower(<u>C_name,Loan_No</u>)\n",
        "\n",
        "## c\n",
        "In Account and Loan, B_name should have a foreign key constraint and a not null constraint\n",
        "\n",
        "In Depositor, Account_No and C_name should have foreign key constraints\n",
        "\n",
        "In Borrower, Loan_No and C_name should have foreign key constraints\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2 \n",
        "## a\n",
        "\n",
        "```{dot}\n",
        "digraph {\n",
        "    rankdir=LR;\n",
        "    node [shape=box];\n",
        "    \n",
        "    /* Entities */\n",
        "    Member [label=\"Member\\n(memberID, name, email)\"];\n",
        "    Address [label=\"Address\\n(addressID, street, city,\\nstate, zip, emergency_phone)\"];\n",
        "    Equipment [label=\"Equipment\\n(equipmentID, type,\\nresistance_level)\"];\n",
        "    FitnessCenter [label=\"FitnessCenter\\n(centerID, name, city,\\nopening_year)\"];\n",
        "    WorkoutSession [label=\"WorkoutSession\\n(sessionID, title,\\ndifficulty_level)\"];\n",
        "    \n",
        "    m[label=\"date, time\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    /* Relationships */\n",
        "    node [shape=diamond];\n",
        "    \n",
        "    lives_at [label=\"lives_at\"];\n",
        "    uses [label=\"uses\"];\n",
        "    offers [label=\"offers\"];\n",
        "    attends [label=\"attends\"];\n",
        "    trainer [label=\"trainer\"];\n",
        "    \n",
        "    /* Connections with cardinalities */\n",
        "    edge [dir=forward]\n",
        "    lives_at -> Address \n",
        "    lives_at -> Address \n",
        "\n",
        "    in -> FitnessCenter\n",
        "    \n",
        "    trainer -> Member \n",
        "    \n",
        "    offers -> FitnessCenter \n",
        "    offers -> FitnessCenter \n",
        "\n",
        "    edge [dir=none]\n",
        "    Equipment -> in\n",
        "    Equipment -> in\n",
        "\n",
        "    lives_at -> Member\n",
        "    lives_at -> Member\n",
        "\n",
        "    Member -> attends \n",
        "\n",
        "    WorkoutSession -> attends \n",
        "    WorkoutSession -> attends \n",
        "\n",
        "    WorkoutSession -> offers \n",
        "    WorkoutSession -> offers \n",
        "    \n",
        "    trainer -> WorkoutSession\n",
        "    trainer -> WorkoutSession\n",
        "\n",
        "    Member -> uses \n",
        "    Equipment -> uses\n",
        "\n",
        "    edge [dir=none, style=dashed]\n",
        "\n",
        "    uses -> m\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Assumptions**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. All Equipments must be in a Fitness Center\n",
        "2. All Fitness Centers must offer at least one Workout Session\n",
        "3. All Workout Sessions must have one trainer, at least one member attending, and be in one fitness center\n",
        "4. All Members have one Address\n",
        "5. All Addresses corresspond to at least one Member\n",
        "6. Member can use a piece of Equipment more than once so a date and time was created\n",
        "\n",
        "## b\n",
        "Equipment(<u>equipmentID</u>, type, resistance_level, centerID)\n",
        "\n",
        "FitnessCenter(<u>centerID</u>, name, city, opening_year, sessionIDs)\n",
        "\n",
        "WorkoutSession(<u>sessionID</u>, title, difficulty_level, trainerID, attendee's IDs, centerID)\n",
        "\n",
        "Member(<u>memberID</u>, name, email, addressID)\n",
        "\n",
        "Address(<u>addressID</u>, street, city, state, zip, emergency_phone, memberIDs)\n",
        "\n",
        "Uses(<u>equipmentID, memberID, date,time</u>)\n",
        "\n",
        "<div style=\"page-break-before:always\">&nbsp;</div> \n",
        "\n",
        "# 3\n",
        "## a\n",
        "\n",
        "```{dot}\n",
        "digraph {\n",
        "    node [shape=box]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Attendee [label=\"Attendee\\n(Attendee_ID, name)\"]\n",
        "    Conference [label=\"Conference\\n(Conference_ID, Conference_Name,\\nDate, Time, Status)\"]\n",
        "    Room [label=\"Room\\n(Room_ID,Room_Name)\"]\n",
        "    Seat [label=\"Seat Number\"]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    node [shape=diamond]\n",
        "\n",
        "    Reg [label=\"Registration\"]\n",
        "    Loc [label=\"Location\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    edge [dir=none]\n",
        "    \n",
        "    Attendee -> Reg\n",
        "\n",
        "    Conference -> Reg\n",
        "\n",
        "    Loc -> Conference\n",
        "    Loc -> Conference\n",
        "    \n",
        "    edge [dir=forward]\n",
        "\n",
        "    Loc -> Room\n",
        "\n",
        "    edge [dir=none, style=dashed]\n",
        "    Reg -> Seat\n",
        "}\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Assumptions**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Seats are numbered specifically for an event\n",
        "2. Attendee only has one seat for an event\n",
        "3. Conference only has one room\n",
        "4. Conference_ID References a Unique instance of a conference (ie if a conference has multiple schedules they have different ids despite having the same name but different times)\n",
        "5. Attendee doesn't need to be regestired to a conference (could be in system from a previous year, maybe they didn't complete all registration steps etc)\n",
        "6. Not all conferences need to have an attendee\n",
        "\n",
        "## b\n",
        "\n",
        "Attendee(<u>Attendee_ID</u>, name)\n",
        "\n",
        "Conference(<u>Conference_ID</u>, Conference_Name, Ddate, Time, Status, Room_ID, Room_Name)\n",
        "\n",
        "Registration(<u>Attendee_ID,Conference_ID</u>, Seat Number)\n",
        "\n",
        "### Constraints\n",
        "Registration should have foreign key constraints on Attendee_ID and Conference_ID and the two should have key constraints as well\n",
        "\n",
        "Attendee and Conference should have key constraints on Attendee_ID and Conference_ID respectively"
      ],
      "id": "8d5fd209"
    }
  ],
